Where is the team secrets vault and how do I request access to it?

There isn't a single "team secrets vault" as a standalone tool — secrets are managed through a few different systems depending on environment:

Where secrets actually live:

    Local development — your own .env file, populated with test/sandbox credentials
    Staging & Production — AWS Secrets Manager, injected into Kubernetes pods automatically
    CI/CD — GitHub Repository Secrets

Direct access to view secret values in AWS Secrets Manager is restricted to team leads. If you need a specific secret value:

    Ask a team lead directly, or
    For staging only, you can inspect a running pod's environment: kubectl exec <pod> -- env | grep <VAR_NAME>

For the "shared team vault" dev credentials mentioned for things like the Nexus development key — that's typically distributed by a team lead rather than something you self-serve from a tool.

To request access to any of these systems (AWS SSO roles, Datadog, PagerDuty, etc.):

    Post in #eng-access on Slack with what system you need, what level (read/write/admin), and why
    Your manager approves in-thread
    An admin grants it and confirms

For anything involving production secrets specifically, you'd also need sign-off from the Director of Engineering in addition to your manager.

